{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"a874ac2f003a87a9","name":"card_event_spy_ring","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/Breakthrough/events/card_event_spy_ring","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"SPY RING","text":"Add a random Research card to your hand.","flavorText":"The Soviet Union had an elaborate ring of secret agents working for them during WWII. One of them was Richard Sorge who worked undercover as a German journalist in both Germany and Japan and provided vital wartime intelligence before he was caught and hanged by the Japanese in 1944. Many of the spies were double agents that had infiltrated, not only the Axis ranks, but also the ranks of the Allies, f.ex. Harold “Kim” Philby, one of the Cambridge Five, who was a senior officer in Britain’s Secret Intelligence Service. Another one was Klaus Fuchs who was the primary physicist on the Manhattan Project and passed on secrets about the A-bomb to Moscow. Many of the Soviet moles continued their work long into the Cold War, most were driven by ideology, but others by money or adventure.","faction":"Soviet","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_spy_ring","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_spy_ring_title","SourceString":"SPY RING","LocalizedString":"SPY RING"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_spy_ring_text","SourceString":"Add a random Research card to your hand.","LocalizedString":"Add a random Research card to your hand."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_spy_ring_history","SourceString":"The Soviet Union had an elaborate ring of secret agents working for them during WWII. One of them was Richard Sorge who worked undercover as a German journalist in both Germany and Japan and provided vital wartime intelligence before he was caught and hanged by the 